<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- 🔴 THE NATIVE PROVIDER IS e_sqlcipher, NOT e_sqlite3, AND THAT IS A DELIBERATE TRADE RECORDED HERE
         RATHER THAN LEFT FOR SOMEONE TO REDISCOVER (census row 16.1, the company vault).

         WHY .Core AND NOT PLAIN Microsoft.Data.Sqlite. The plain package takes a HARD dependency on
         SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlite3, and two bundles in one graph both publish the type
         SQLitePCL.Batteries_V2 — which provider actually wins then depends on assembly resolution order
         rather than on anything written down. Microsoft.Data.Sqlite.Core carries no bundle, so the single
         PackageReference below is the only provider in the graph and the choice is explicit.

         WHY e_sqlcipher AT ALL. Page-level encryption cannot be done above the provider: the company name is
         itself company data the vault must hide, and it lives in a row of the company .db. SQLCipher encrypts
         every page including the schema, so nothing readable survives in the file. An UNKEYED database opens
         under this provider exactly as before, which is why the ~40 schema/migration tests that open
         databases directly needed no change at all.

         🔴 THE COST, STATED PLAINLY. bundle_e_sqlite3 was pinned to 3.0.3 to escape advisory NU1903 on
         SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3 2.1.11. The e_sqlcipher family STOPS at 2.1.11 — there is no 3.x — so this
         swap moves the native back to that vintage (SQLCipher 4.5.2 community). `dotnet restore` raises NO
         NU1903 here, because the advisory is filed against the e_sqlite3 package id and not against
         e_sqlcipher; the audit being silent is NOT the same as the code being newer. This is a user decision
         and it is reported as one. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Data.Sqlite.Core" Version="10.0.9" />
    <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlcipher" Version="2.1.11" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Apex.Ledger\Apex.Ledger.csproj" />
    <!-- The SMTP-profile repository port (RQ-27) and its capture-only SmtpProfile value live in Apex.Ledger.Io
         (framework-agnostic, no password). Referenced so this adapter can implement ISmtpProfileRepository. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Apex.Ledger.Io\Apex.Ledger.Io.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
